From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:14:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/dp: Flush the CRC worker before stopping the sink CRC

drm_dp_stop_crc() clears DP_TEST_SINK_START first and flushes the CRC
worker after that. The worker may still be in a loop iteration: after
-EAGAIN it sleeps for 1 to 2 ms and reads the sink a second time
without checking crtc->crc.opened again, and that read finds
TEST_SINK_START cleared and hits the WARN_ON() in drm_dp_aux_get_crc().
With a sink that does not report a new CRC every frame, most reads
return -EAGAIN, so closing the CRC file often lands in that sleep.

Flush the worker first. The CRC debugfs code clears crtc->crc.opened
before it calls set_crc_source() to stop the capture, so the worker
leaves its loop at the next check, and both of its reads run while the
sink still has TEST_SINK_START set.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S (Allwinner A733) with a DisplayPort
monitor: a capture closed after its first CRC warns in
drm_dp_aux_get_crc(), called from the retry in drm_dp_aux_crc_work().

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: CRC captures closed at random points of the
frame no longer warn, and every capture still returns its CRC.

Fixes: 79c1da7c3bf7 ("drm/dp: add helpers for capture of frame CRCs")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
index 488fd123a01a..f9e65bd266cf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c
@@ -2507,6 +2507,12 @@ int drm_dp_stop_crc(struct drm_dp_aux *aux)
 	u8 buf;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The worker reads the sink until crtc->crc.opened is cleared, so
+	 * let it finish before the sink stops.
+	 */
+	flush_work(&aux->crc_work);
+
 	ret = drm_dp_dpcd_read_byte(aux, DP_TEST_SINK, &buf);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
@@ -2515,7 +2521,6 @@ int drm_dp_stop_crc(struct drm_dp_aux *aux)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	flush_work(&aux->crc_work);
 	aux->crtc = NULL;
 
 	return 0;
